# Secrets. Env files are per-clone, including .env.1password: its references
# name vault items and their paths. `task setup:secrets` writes .env.mcp (the
# MCP tokens) from it. Only the .example contract is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.mcp.example

# Claude Code MCP servers are registered per user by `task setup:mcp`, not here.
.mcp.json

